lication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 12 & 16 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c91fb2b-5607-555d-b897-f0e76765dfa6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Lower Triangular Matrix Given the Elementary Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c8ce5b-bcdc-5878-9197-4aa163f4f917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117307} {:answer/id #uuid "946def1f-e154-5ab2-a64a-da0922dfd887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117308} {:answer/id #uuid "b5894b30-952b-5739-82c7-d02ab9c3342b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117309} {:answer/id #uuid "523ef849-046c-5f94-95d8-57aa901cfa01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \